# Rust
/target
target
/crates/peridot/target/

# The root Cargo.lock is deliberately tracked: a plugin and the runtime that loads it must
# resolve against one identical lockfile, so it is part of the plugin contract, not just
# hygiene. Per-member lockfiles are not — they only appear when a crate is built outside the
# workspace, which is exactly what the plugin ABI forbids.
crates/**/Cargo.lock

# CMake output from the c-wasm guest modules. CMakeLists.txt files are tracked; everything
# CMake generates from them is not.
cmake-build*
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.DS_Store
